---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us — PTCL Speed Test"
  description="About PTCL Speed Test: a free, independent tool for checking PTCL broadband speed in Pakistan, with honest guides on what your results mean."
  canonical="/about"
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</p>
      <h1>About PTCL Speed Test</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A free, independent tool to check your PTCL internet speed — and understand what
        the numbers actually mean.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>What this site does</h2>
      <p>
        This site runs a real speed test in your browser: it measures your download
        speed, upload speed, ping and jitter against the nearest test server, in under 30
        seconds. No account, no app, no sign-up.
      </p>
      <p>
        Around the test, you'll find plain-English guides: how to read your results, how
        to squeeze more speed out of your PTCL connection, and what ping and jitter mean
        for gaming and video calls. The goal is simple — help you know whether you're
        getting the speed you pay for, and what to do if you're not.
      </p>

      <h2>How the test works</h2>
      <p>
        The test runs entirely in your browser. It sends small timing requests to measure
        ping and jitter, then downloads and uploads test data for a few seconds each to
        measure throughput. Test traffic goes to the nearest Cloudflare edge server. Your
        results are shown to you immediately, and a short history is kept only in your own
        browser — we never see your results.
      </p>

      <h2>Independent and unaffiliated</h2>
      <p>
        This site is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Pakistan
        Telecommunication Company Limited (PTCL), Etisalat, or any other internet service
        provider. "PTCL" is used only to describe whose customers this tool is made for.
        For official packages, billing and complaints, contact PTCL directly on helpline
        1218 or at ptcl.com.pk.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and limits</h2>
      <p>
        Speed tests measure your connection at a moment in time. Results vary with Wi-Fi
        signal, other devices, time of day and server load — that's why we recommend
        testing over Ethernet and running the test a few times. The test is a useful
        indicator, not a lab measurement, and it can't diagnose faults inside PTCL's
        network.
      </p>

      <p><a href="/contact">Questions or feedback? Contact us →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
